stream
BT /F1 9 Tf 34 754 Td 11 TL
(KESTREL POINT CONTAINER TERMINAL) Tj T*
(BERTH OPERATIONS MEMORANDUM) Tj T*
(shift KP-2042-S23    reference QCR-829677) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 1  CONTROL VALUES ISSUED HERE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These three values are issued here and are carried in no other paper) Tj T*
(of this shift. The first two govern the quay ration; the third) Tj T*
(governs the dependency stage. The fourth value the quay ration needs,) Tj T*
(the damping fraction, is issued by the capacity workbook.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  ration_pass_budget          5) Tj T*
(  ration_minimum_step         3 crane minutes) Tj T*
(  dependency_protection_depth 2) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The pass budget is a count of passes, not a convergence test. The) Tj T*
(ration stops when the budget is spent whether or not the shares have) Tj T*
(settled, and the shares as they stand at that point are the shares) Tj T*
(that get published.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The minimum step is the smallest move a share may make in one pass.) Tj T*
(A share whose damped move rounds to nothing still moves by the) Tj T*
(minimum step toward its target, so a share that has not reached its) Tj T*
(target never sits still while passes remain.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 2  REHANDLE SURCHARGE LADDER) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  tier_depth   surcharge_cents) Tj T*
(  1            0) Tj T*
(  2            450) Tj T*
(  3            900) Tj T*
(  4            1600) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A tier depth beyond the last rung of the ladder carries the surcharge) Tj T*
(of the last rung. A tier depth of one carries no surcharge.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 3  QUAY GANG ROSTER) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The gang roster is the minute allowance the quay can actually crew in) Tj T*
(each slot. The berth window register declares what the berth asked) Tj T*
(for. The pool a berth rations in a slot is the smaller of the two.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  berth_id     slot_code  gang_code  gang_minutes) Tj T*
(  bt_alder     SL01       GNG-1      6) Tj T*
